  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "On a volume invariant of 3-manifolds (Kegel, Ray, Spreer, Thompson, Tillmann) — defines topological volume vol_t(M), the smallest volume of a hyperbolic-link complement in M; bounds and a…\n\n**On a volume invariant of 3-manifolds** — Marc Kegel, Arunima Ray, Jonathan Spreer, Em Thompson, Stephan Tillmann.\n\nIntroduces the **topological volume** vol_t(M): for a 3-manifold M, the smallest volume of the complement of a (possibly empty) hyperbolic link in M. Gives refinements of the invariant, asymptotically tight upper and lower bounds, and classifies all non-hyperbolic closed 3-manifolds with topological volume at most 3.07.\n\n**Why it may bear here.** A volume invariant defined for *non-hyperbolic* manifolds is exactly the gap this corpus hits when a knot is non-hyperbolic and its hyperbolic volume is zero (the trefoil case). Whether that gap is the one this invariant fills is unexamined.",
      "lang": "en",
